[Music]  this morning in our school matters  series we're focusing on a very heated  issue that's become a big old flash  point in the debate over how to respond  to this pandemic we're talking about  mask mandates for students now some  school board meetings have turned into  confrontations between opponents and  supporters of the move a recent cbs news  poll found this only six percent of  parents say that mass mandates should  not be allowed while 58 percent say they  should absolutely be required 36 believe  mass should be optional but the voices  of those opponents are often the loudest  new jersey governor recently announced a  mass mandate for all schools and  employees were told to get vaccinated or  face covet test  meg oliver went to 110 school board  meeting in wayne new jersey  [Music]  the science says that kids do not carry  this stuff they do not spread it even  before the school board meeting in wayne  new jersey began families against the  school mask mandates gathered outside to  loudly protest why are you guys here  tonight to get mass off of  us  this school is it worth it to wear a  mask if it means your school is going to  open  no  i'm protesting for my body my choice  because  i believe that if someone wants to wear  a mask then they can wear a mask because  like it's their body and they get to  choose but also if someone doesn't  really want to wear a mask then people  don't really have the right to force it  on them so if you had a choice to wear a  mask and go to school or stay at home  what would it be  i would  i would want to wear a mask and go to  school actually but  that's actually a really tough question  that's a tough question right because  that's where we go to school  then we're being forced to wear a mask  but if we're staying at home then we're  being forced to stay at home  [Music]  the majority of the nearly 100 people at  this school board meeting were there to  express their frustration with new  jersey's school mask mandate and demand  the district stand up to the governor  science is not  fact  science is meant to be challenged there  is no pandemic amongst children  the young lady just said that there is  no pandemic among the children  the lady is either in denial or she's  just lying  because every newspaper excuse me i have  the microphone  the lady is misinformed or she is lying  you should be embarrassed and ashamed  with the agenda that all of you are  letting happening in this town there is  a well-orchestrated  well-coordinated  uh and loud movement of people here  i think it's important that you hear  uh from parents as well who support  the governor's mask mandate for k-12  schools now i support anyone who wants  to wear a mask that is their choice to  do so but if i'm going to respect their  right they need to respect mine i will  be telling both my boys not to wear  masks thank you  do you feel you're accomplishing  something with these meetings  well they're not optional uh whether i  feel we're accomplishing um i think it's  our job i think we were elected to serve  the community and part of that is  listening  we wanted to hear more from parents who  spoke out so we met up with dana aliquin  at a local park she's the mother of two  young children one who is autistic she's  not vaccinated and her kids are too  young to receive the shot  you were very vocal at this board  meeting what was your goal  really just to speak for the kids  i  personally  do not want to send my child with a mask  that's  you know my and my husband's  opinion there are no studies  done or being done  about the longevity of mask wearing in  children is there a world where you  would consider putting a mask on your  child to go to school this fall  not this fall do you believe that masks  can help reduce the transmission of  covet  if they're worn properly they can the  kids aren't wearing them properly and  that's also my big concern but if they  do wear them properly would you consider  sending your kids to school with the  mask um this year no because i just  think that my daughter went through it  last year it took a mental toll i think  it's hard for these kids to learn how to  read learn how to  do a lot of their lessons when their  teachers mouths are covered by the mask  and their peers masks it's a little  dehumanizing  a lot of people will argue that you're  part of a community and being part of a  community  you want to protect others by masking  and vaccinating what's your response to  that um i agree with that but the only  thing  to counter is  these people that don't feel safe  you know they're still going out food  shopping they're still going out to  concerts they're gonna they're still  going to the mall they're still going to  the beach if they were that terrified i  feel that if they felt that threatened i  feel that  they would be staying home and i don't  think that everyone collectively needs  to be punished for that but now you're  gonna  during our interview a local parent who  supports mass mandates recognized dana  yeah being loud  those opposing the school mask mandate  and those who support it have competing  petitions circulating online those who  support masks currently have around 700  more signatures  i wrote the opposing  petition by the way that has more  signatures than yours  this was their least appealing yeah and  most people agree with us  there's a a lot going on here  that's fine it's despicable okay you're  entitled to your opinion and i'm  entitled to mine are you vaccinated no  why not  shame on you  shame on you  i think a lot of people are going to  paint a picture of you if you're getting  up at a board meeting speaking that your  anti-mask your anti-vaccine  your anti-all these things is that  accurate no we  are not anti-anything we are fighting  for our god-given right  to choose what is best for our children  [Music]  in the past month the number of kids  contracting covid went from close to 40  000 to 180 000 by the end of last week  experts say if masks are worn properly  along with vaccinations ventilation and  testing they can help reduce the  transmission of covid in the classroom  and i have to say you know i called top  uh three of the top doctors across the  country yesterday to talk about some of  the things that these parents said and  they agreed that if we're not putting  these masks on our children the right  way  they're not effective so if you're going  to hand an adult mask to a kid this fall  turn the sides make sure it fits yeah i  thought that was a good take away i mean  as a parent i understand you don't even  if another parent tells my kids not to  run around the pool i'm like hey i got  it i got it right you don't want that  kind of interference but you know the  experts are saying this for a reason  they've been saying it for a long time  now it's clear it's settled it's  interesting to see the exchange between  the two parents because did their kids  know each other no but they were playing  together before our interview started  and they didn't realize it before the  kids went away  oh boy meg thank you very much

